From there, we calculate according to: $(1)^3[(cos(t))^6 + (1 - (cos(t))^2)^{3}] = 7/16$ ;

or  $(cos(t))^6 + 1 - 3(cos(t))^2 + 3(cos(t))^4 - (cos(t))^6 = 7/16$ ;

or  $3(cos(t))^4 - 3(cos(t))^2 + 9/16 = 0$ ;

or  $48(cos(t))^4 - 48(cos(t))^2 + 9 = 0$ ;

or  $16(cos(t))^4  - 16(cos(t))^2 + 3 = 0$ ;

or  $[4(cos(t))^2 - 1][4(cos(t))^2 - 3] = 0$ ;

or  $(cos(t))^2 = 1/4, 3/4$ ;

or  $cos(t) =  \pm1/2 \pm \sqrt{3}/2$ which occur at the angles  $t = \pi/6, \pi/3, 2\pi/3, 5\pi/6, 7\pi/6, 4\pi/3, 5\pi/3,11\pi/6$ .  Hence, our set of real solutions include the ordered pairs  $(x, y) = (r*cos(t), r*sin(t))$ : $(\sqrt{3}/2, 1/2); (1/2, \sqrt{3}/2); (-1/2, \sqrt{3}/2); (-\sqrt{3}/2, 1/2); (-\sqrt{3}/2, -1/2); (-1/2, -\sqrt{3}/2); (1/2, -\sqrt{3}/2); (\sqrt{3}/2, -1/2)$ .

